  "task": "Prepare our school's comprehensive annual academic report. This is a multi-sheet workbook: calculate graduation rates, GPA distributions, test score summaries, and attendance statistics on separate sheets, then build a dashboard overview sheet with key metrics pulled from each section, protect the formula sheets, and set up the whole workbook for professional printing. The file to work on is /home/user/calc_edu_comprehensive_annual_report_070_initial.xlsx.\n\nRequirements (every item is checked):\n1. Keep the existing sheet names: Graduation, GPAData, TestScores, Attendance, Dashboard. On each data sheet, put the analysis in column F (labels) and column G (formulas).\n2. Graduation: F2 holds a label (e.g. \"Graduation Rate\"); G2 is a COUNTIF formula that counts graduated students (criterion \"Y\" in the Graduated column), e.g. =COUNTIF(C2:C26,\"Y\") or a rate built on it; G4 is an AVERAGEIF formula giving the average Years to Graduate of graduates.\n3. GPAData: G2 = COUNTIF formula for the top GPA band (4.0); G3 = COUNTIFS formula for GPA 3.0-3.99; G4 = COUNTIFS formula for GPA 2.0-2.99; G5 = COUNTIF formula for GPA below 2.0.\n4. TestScores: G2 = AVERAGE of Math scores, G3 = AVERAGE of Reading scores (G4 = AVERAGE of Science scores); G7, G8 and G9 = COUNTIF formulas counting proficient students (score >= 70) for Math, Reading and Science (the criterion must contain 70, e.g. \">=70\").\n5. Attendance: F2 holds a label (e.g. \"Avg Attendance Rate\"); G2 is an AVERAGE-based formula for the average attendance rate; G3 is a COUNTIF formula counting chronically absent students (attendance below 90%).\n6. Dashboard: A1 holds a bold report title; bold section labels in A4 (Graduation), A10 (GPA), A17 (Test Scores) and A23 (Attendance); key metrics under each section are formulas referencing the analysis cells on the other sheets, with at least one reference to each of Graduation!, GPAData!, TestScores! and Attendance!; at least 10 non-empty cells in total; a print area is set on the Dashboard sheet.\n7. Sheet protection is enabled on Graduation, GPAData, TestScores and Attendance (a password is optional).\n8. Save the workbook in place at the same path, keeping the .xlsx format.",
